  "id": "tactile-illusion",
  "term": "tactile illusion",
  "definition": "A tactile illusion is a false impression arising in touch, usually during active touching and often mixed with sensations of movement. It can make motion over the skin seem greater or wrongly directed, or make a touched body part seem to move when something passes across it.",
